The camera pans across a stone‑walled tavern lit by flickering torches. A wooden bar stretches from one side to the other. In front of it stands Amy, a medium‑statured woman in a simple linen apron, holding a mug of amber ale with both hands. She smiles at an elf perched on a stool and nods politely.

Amy lifts a wooden jug, pours its contents into a crystal goblet held by the elf, then sets the goblet down beside the elf’s elbow. The goblet clinks against the bar as the elf takes a sip.

A dwarf enters the tavern, steps onto a low table, and sits with a thud of his boots on the wooden floorboards. Amy walks from behind the bar to the table, places a bowl of steaming stew in front of him, then returns to the bar.

An orc strides up to the counter; Amy wipes his palm against her apron before handing him a pint of golden mead. The orc clinks its mug against the bar and nods thanks.

The bell above the door rings again as more magical humanoid creatures—an elf, a dwarf, an orc, a goblin—enter one by one, each taking their seat at tables around the tavern. Amy moves from table to table, refilling mugs, setting plates down, wiping counters with her apron.

The camera pulls back to show all of the patrons laughing and drinking in the bustling tavern while Amy stands behind the bar, a satisfied smile on her face as she watches the magical humanoid creatures enjoy their evening.
